key E

#Notes
// Closing arrangement from the workbook's “Turn It Up (closing)” tab.
// The workbook marks A and C#m as optional passing chords on the second and fourth verse lines; the E-to-B move below is the simple path.
> Order: soft loop and thanksgiving, lead-guitar intro x2, verse 1, pre-chorus, chorus x2, outro, ending swell.

#Loop
> Soft E–A–C#m–B loop. Thank the Lord and praise Him once again.
E A C#m B

#i x2
> Lead guitar enters; full band in. Play twice.
E A C#m B

#v
>vox All voices.
E.. A.. C#m.. B..
_You are _here as we _lift you _up
E B
You are _riding on our _praise
E.. A.. C#m.. B..
_Be enthroned _over _everything _
E B
You are _seated in our _praise

#p
> Build with fills on “I am free!”
C#m B
_This is prophetic I can _feel it in the air
A B
_We lift our praise and you _change the atmosphere
C#m B
_With hearts open now _everybody singing out
A B
_I am _free!

#c x2
> Full band; sing the chorus twice.
E B
Turn it _up this sound of _praise
A
Make it _louder than any other
E B C#m.. A.. B
Lift him _up and shout his _name over _all _ _

#o
> Full band on A; finish with a swell on E and “Thank you!”
A
E
